      "0": [
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe DOM/URL explicitly supports that a custom UTC time window was set (starttime/endtime present) and that UTC is the basis (`timeZone=utc` plus row timestamps labeled `(UTC)`). It also explicitly supports min magnitude 4.5 (`minmagnitude`: 4.5). However, “worldwide” scope is not explicitly stated as such in the DOM, and while the search JSON shows no explicit region/bounding-box filter, the URL also contains `extent=...` parameters (map viewport) and the DOM snapshot alone does not explicitly confirm that no geographic constraint affected the query.",
          "discrepancies": "Worldwide geographic scope is inferred from absence of region params in `search` JSON, but not explicitly labeled/confirmed as “Worldwide” in the DOM snapshot.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 11. URL includes: `timeZone=utc` and `search={\"name\":\"Search Results\",\"params\":{\"starttime\":\"2026-09-08 00:00:00\",\"endtime\":\"2026-09-09 00:00:00\",\"minmagnitude\":4.5,\"orderby\":\"magnitude\"}}`. Visible list rows show timestamps suffixed with `(UTC)` (e.g., `2026-09-08 23:23:42 (UTC)`). No explicit region parameter is shown inside the `search` JSON params beyond start/end/minmagnitude/orderby.",
          "screenshot_idx": 11,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 11
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nCriterion 0 requires evidence that the correct USGS query filters were applied (custom UTC 24h range, worldwide region, min magnitude 4.5+). The DOM evidence (STATE_INDEX 0) confirms the presence of the necessary controls and that UTC is the intended basis for the date fields (\"Start (UTC)\", \"End (UTC)\") and that worldwide region options exist (\"World\"/\"Worldwide\"), and that a \"4.5+\" magnitude option exists. However, it does not show that \"Custom\" was selected, does not show the actual start/end values entered, does not show magnitude set to 4.5+, and does not show that any geographic restriction remained worldwide. Therefore the criterion is only partially supported by the available DOM-model state.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s claimed applied parameters (custom UTC range 2026-09-08 00:00:00 to 2026-09-09 00:00:00; min magnitude 4.5; worldwide; orderby=magnitude) are not verifiable from DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 0 because it shows only default/placeholder input content (e.g., Start input placeholder \"yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss\" and Minimum magnitude evidence \"2.5\") and no selected state or results. No DOM evidence is provided for the final map URL parameters or any post-search state.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 0 (URL: https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/search/, Title: \"Search Earthquake Catalog\") shows the search form contains explicit UTC date-time controls and worldwide geographic scope options:\n- Under \"Date & Time\" it lists \"Custom\" with fields labeled \"Start (UTC)\" and \"End (UTC)\" (actions: [5] text-input \"yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss\").\n- Under \"Geographic Region\" it lists options including \"World\" and also separately shows \"Worldwide\".\n- Under \"Magnitude\" it lists preset options including \"4.5+\" and a \"Minimum\" text input showing evidence value \"2.5\".\nThis DOM snapshot does not display any selected/checked state, entered custom date values, or any results/ordering state.",
          "screenshot_idx": 0,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 0
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe DOM explicitly supports that the page provides UTC-based custom time range inputs (\"Date & Time Start (UTC)\" / \"End (UTC)\") and that the Geographic Region includes a worldwide option (\"World\" / text \"Worldwide\"). However, the DOM snapshot does not confirm the specific required filter settings were actually applied: it does not show the selected magnitude threshold as \"4.5+\" (and the only explicit magnitude value evidence shown is \"Magnitude Minimum\" = \"2.5\"), it does not show the entered Start/End UTC values, and it does not show any applied ordering by magnitude. Therefore, only the availability (not the successful application) of key filter controls is evidenced here.",
          "discrepancies": "Agent claims filters/ordering were applied (UTC window 2026-09-08 00:00:00 to 2026-09-09 00:00:00; min magnitude 4.5; worldwide; orderby=magnitude). DOM state 6 does not display those entered UTC values, does not show \"4.5+\" as selected, and instead shows \"Magnitude Minimum\" evidence value \"2.5\". Ordering by magnitude is also not evidenced in this DOM snapshot.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 6 (https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/search/)\n- Date & Time section explicitly shows UTC fields: text-input labeled \"Date & Time Start (UTC)\" and text-input labeled \"Date & Time End (UTC)\".\n- Geographic Region section shows options including \"World\" and the presence of text \"Worldwide\".\n- Magnitude section shows options \"2.5+\", \"4.5+\", and also a \"Magnitude Minimum\" text-input with visible evidence value \"2.5\".\n- This DOM snapshot does not display any selected/checked state for \"4.5+\" nor does it show the filled contents of the Start/End (UTC) textboxes.\n- There is a visible \"Search\" button, but no results list, no applied filter summary, and no output ordering control/value in this snapshot.",
          "screenshot_idx": 6,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 6
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nCriterion 0 requires confirming that the query filters were correctly applied (custom preceding-24-hours UTC range, worldwide, min magnitude 4.5+). The DOM snapshot (State 3) supports that the page provides UTC date/time inputs (“Date & Time Start (UTC)”) and includes worldwide geographic controls (“Worldwide”) and a “4.5+” magnitude option, but it does not explicitly show that these were selected/applied (no checked/selected state is shown, and no filled start/end values are present in the DOM evidence). Therefore the DOM supports availability of the correct filter controls and UTC basis, but not that the specific magnitude threshold, worldwide scope, and exact 24-hour UTC range were actually applied.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s narrative claims filters were applied with a specific custom UTC range (2026-09-08 00:00:00 to 2026-09-09 00:00:00) and magnitude ≥4.5 worldwide, but DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 3 does not display the entered start/end values nor any selected/checked state for “4.5+” or “Worldwide”, so those applied-filter facts are not provable from this DOM snapshot.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
