          "screenshot_idx": 3,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 3
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThis DOM snapshot supports that the agent reached the USGS Search form state where a Custom UTC date-time range can be set (explicit labels “Start (UTC)” and “Date & Time Start (UTC)” input are present, and “Custom” is shown under Date & Time). It also shows that worldwide region options (“World” / “Worldwide”) are available.\nHowever, the criterion requires that the query filters are correctly applied (custom preceding-24-hours UTC range, min magnitude ≥4.5, worldwide, and—per task context—ordering by magnitude). In DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 2, the only explicit field value shown is “Magnitude Minimum” evidence: 2.5 (not 4.5), and the DOM does not display the entered Start/End UTC values or any order-by setting. Therefore, the DOM provides only partial support for the criterion (UI capability/state to set the filters, but not confirmation they were applied as required).",
          "discrepancies": "- Magnitude threshold: DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 2 shows “Magnitude Minimum” evidence value \"2.5\", which does not match the required ≥4.5.\n- UTC 24-hour range: DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 2 shows the presence of “Start (UTC)” and “End (UTC)” controls but does not show populated values, so it cannot confirm the specific 24-hour range was applied.\n- Worldwide region: DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 2 shows worldwide options exist, but does not confirm the selected value is worldwide.\n- Ordering by magnitude: no order-by control/value is visible in DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 2, so ordering cannot be confirmed from this snapshot.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 2 (https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/search/)\n- Under “Date & Time”, the form shows “Custom” selected (context lists options “Past 7 Days”, “Past 30 Days”, “Custom”) and exposes fields labeled:\n  - “Start (UTC)” with a text-input: \"Date & Time Start (UTC)\" (actions: click,type,focus)\n  - “End (UTC)” (label present; input not shown in this snapshot)\n- Under “Magnitude”, the UI shows preset options including “4.5+” and also shows a numeric minimum field:\n  - text-input “Magnitude Minimum” with evidence value: \"2.5\"\n- Under “Geographic Region”, the UI presents region options including “World” / “Worldwide” (i.e., worldwide region is available on the form).\n(From this DOM snapshot alone, no filled-in custom start/end values, no confirmed min magnitude=4.5 selection, and no order-by control/value are shown.)",
